posts.body:
@Robro33
figured out what's going on here, so I'll see if I can help get this wrapped up
.
You lost STAB but gained an immunity because you're no longer getting that +50%, so once you add that back in, you're going to lose the immunity again.
--------------
I think what you're going to need to do, to have both STAB and immunities using Visustella, is modify the math in JS: Finalize Rate within Element Rulings in the ElementStatusCore ->
// Declare Constants
const target = arguments[0];
const action = this;
const elements = action.elements();
const targetRate = action.calcTargetElementRate(target, elements);
const sign = targetRate >= 0 ? 1 : -1;
const base = Math.abs(targetRate);
const plus = action.calcUserElementDamagePlus(target, elements);
const rate = action.calcUserElementDamageRate(target, elements);
const flat = action.calcUserElementDamageFlat(target, elements);
// Determine Return Value
return sign * Math.max((base + plus) * rate + flat, 0);;
This is how it looks baseline I believe (I don't think I've made any modifications here, but I did rework some stat calculations elsewhere). If you modify the calculations here, you'll be able to get your elements working how you wish.
Try changing
const sign = targetRate >= 0 ? 1 : -1;
to this:
const sign = targetRate;
and seeing what happens.
--------------
I tested it on my end, and it works just how you would want it.
Characters with +50% elemental damage do 0 damage to a character with an immunity, but keep that +50% otherwise.
NOTE:
If you make this change, I believe it
probably will
break Absorb Element mechanics (i.e. if something was supposed to absorb Electric damage to heal itself, this change might break that effect). This is because
sign
is no longer able to be assigned a -1 to reverse the damage.
Note2:
If you want to know a little more about what I did here, I modified the calculation for
sign
so that it equals exactly to the Trait setting in the database, rather than have an if / else statement that was assigning a 1 to
sign
even if the Trait was set to 0%.

